            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nIf completion is triggered, it is likely that user wants to see the completion entries. How built-in popup is positioned is somewhat out of control for 'mini.completion'. The effect can be minimized by using `vim.o.pumheight = 10` which will likely show completion popup below the cursor line (while signature is likely to be above it).\n\nIn this particular case, the setup LuaLS treats `(` as a trigger character and thus completion triggered. You can adjust it by setting appropriate capability. For example, add the following `on_attach` field to `require(\"lspconfig\").lua_ls.setup()` argument:\n\n```lua\n\ton_attach = function(client, bufnr)\n\t\t-- Reduce unnecessarily long list of completion triggers for better\n\t\t-- 'mini.completion' experience\n\t\tclient.server_capabilities.completionProvider.triggerCharacters = { \".\", \":\" }\n\tend,\n```\n\nClosing as not really an issue with 'mini.completion'.",
